WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.898 --> 00:00:17.439
could hardly believe that Nora had outsmarted them.

2
00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.921
She had led them into the neighbors' yard and then disappeared.

3
00:00:21.841 --> 00:00:23.402
But he wasn't ready to give up yet.

4
00:00:23.422 --> 00:00:27.584
"I have an idea," he told Maggie, Cole, and Nathan.

5
00:00:28.708 --> 00:00:31.929
"Nora probably waited for us to start looking for her.

6
00:00:32.909 --> 00:00:34.970
Then she sneaked back through the hedges.

7
00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.951
If we hurry, we might be able to find her before she makes it to the house."

8
00:00:42.032 --> 00:00:42.832
Nathan nodded.

9
00:00:42.852 --> 00:00:45.313
"Let's go," he said.

10
00:00:46.373 --> 00:00:49.634
He led The Lemonade Detectives through the hedge into his own yard.

11
00:00:50.674 --> 00:00:53.975
They got there just in time to see Nora racing toward the house.

12
00:00:55.515 --> 00:00:56.516
"Stop right there!"

13
00:00:56.916 --> 00:00:57.996
Nathan yelled loudly.

14
00:00:59.116 --> 00:01:00.096
"We caught you, Nora!"

15
00:01:01.077 --> 00:01:02.037
They ran toward her.

16
00:01:02.998 --> 00:01:06.499
Just then the back door flew open and Nora's parents rushed out.

17
00:01:06.519 --> 00:01:08.140
"Oh no!"

18
00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:09.760
Nora's mom exclaimed.

19
00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:11.961
"She got out again!"

20
00:01:13.102 --> 00:01:14.422
Nora's dad looked worried.

21
00:01:14.442 --> 00:01:19.344
"Hush, don't wake her," he told his wife.

22
00:01:20.665 --> 00:01:23.806
"Someone told me you're never supposed to wake a sleepwalker."

23
00:01:24.967 --> 00:01:26.687
"She's not really sleepwalking, Dad!"

24
00:01:27.028 --> 00:01:27.688
Nathan said.

25
00:01:28.832 --> 00:01:30.412
Henry had been watching Nora.

26
00:01:31.593 --> 00:01:36.114
As soon as she'd seen her parents, she'd closed her eyes and held out both arms in front

27
00:01:36.154 --> 00:01:36.434
of her.

28
00:01:37.895 --> 00:01:40.755
Henry thought she looked more like a zombie than a sleepwalker.

29
00:01:41.776 --> 00:01:43.936
But her act seemed to be fooling her parents.

30
00:01:43.956 --> 00:01:49.058
"That's not a nice thing to say, son," Nathan's father scolded.

31
00:01:49.078 --> 00:01:53.979
"Your sister could get hurt if she keeps sleepwalking like this.

32
00:01:55.119 --> 00:01:57.260
I wonder how she got outside this time."

33
00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:01.101
"She climbed out her bedroom window," Nathan said.

34
00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:06.724
"That's enough, Nathan," his father said.

35
00:02:06.744 --> 00:02:09.365
"This is no time for jokes."

36
00:02:10.485 --> 00:02:15.387
"Come with me, sweetie," Nora's mother said softly as she started guiding Nora toward the house.

37
00:02:16.548 --> 00:02:18.269
"Let's get you safely back to bed."

38
00:02:18.289 --> 00:02:22.971
"It's time for you to come inside too," Nathan's father told Nathan.

39
00:02:23.911 --> 00:02:26.212
Then he glanced at Henry, Maggie, and Cole.

40
00:02:27.624 --> 00:02:29.425
"And you kids had better head home.

41
00:02:30.465 --> 00:02:31.125
It's getting late."

42
00:02:31.945 --> 00:02:36.186
"Late? It's not even eight o'clock yet," Maggie said.

43
00:02:37.187 --> 00:02:40.788
Henry grabbed his cousin by the arm and pulled her toward the front of the house.

44
00:02:40.808 --> 00:02:45.749
"Yes, we'd better go," he told Nathan's dad politely.

45
00:02:45.769 --> 00:02:47.970
"See you tomorrow, Nathan."

46
00:02:53.291 --> 00:02:59.030
Now that Nora had been caught "sleepwalking" again, Henry guessed that her parents would watch her very closely.

47
00:03:00.091 --> 00:03:02.994
She probably wouldn't be able to sneak out again that night.

48
00:03:04.134 --> 00:03:07.978
That meant any more detective work would have to wait until the next day.

49
00:03:12.641 --> 00:03:17.345
The following morning Henry was eating breakfast when Maggie hurried in through the kitchen door.

50
00:03:17.365 --> 00:03:22.890
"Good morning, Maggie," said Henry's mother, who was also Maggie's aunt.

51
00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:25.452
"Would you like some scrambled eggs?"

52
00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:27.861
"No thanks, Aunt Susan.

53
00:03:28.681 --> 00:03:29.462
I already ate."

54
00:03:30.482 --> 00:03:33.024
Maggie sat down at the table across from her cousin.

55
00:03:33.044 --> 00:03:36.045
"Hurry up, Henry," she said.

56
00:03:36.065 --> 00:03:40.207
"I want to go back to Nora and Nathan's house and investigate."

57
00:03:41.348 --> 00:03:42.989
"Okay," Henry said.

58
00:03:43.009 --> 00:03:46.051
"Let's call Cole and tell him to meet us there."

59
00:03:49.993 --> 00:03:53.675
Nathan was waiting in front of his house when the three detectives got there.

60
00:03:53.695 --> 00:03:55.936
"What's the plan for today?"

61
00:03:56.372 --> 00:03:56.892
he asked.

62
00:03:58.013 --> 00:04:01.115
"Do you have any theories about what Nora is doing when she sneaks out?"

63
00:04:02.155 --> 00:04:03.876
"Not yet," Henry admitted.

64
00:04:03.896 --> 00:04:07.058
"But at least we know she's not sleepwalking."

65
00:04:08.439 --> 00:04:09.199
Cole nodded.

66
00:04:09.219 --> 00:04:13.182
"She was wide-awake when she ran away from us, that's for sure."

67
00:04:13.202 --> 00:04:18.304
"I still think she was heading for the tree house when she heard us," Maggie said.

68
00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:21.926
"Maybe we should search for clues up there."

69
00:04:22.967 --> 00:04:24.348
Nathan seemed doubtful.

70
00:04:25.752 --> 00:04:28.234
"Why would she sneak around just to go to my tree house?"

71
00:04:28.715 --> 00:04:29.255
he asked.

72
00:04:30.396 --> 00:04:35.140
"She's allowed to climb up there whenever she wants, as long as she tells someone where she's going."

73
00:04:36.221 --> 00:04:37.502
"Really?" Cole said.

74
00:04:37.522 --> 00:04:41.705
"My friend Bruce never lets his little sisters in his tree house."

75
00:04:41.725 --> 00:04:47.390
"Nathan must be much nicer than your friend Bruce," Maggie said with a laugh.

76
00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:51.053
"Anyway, I still think we should look in the tree house."

77
00:04:52.174 --> 00:04:54.216
"You're right, Maggie," Henry agreed.

78
00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:57.282
"It's worth checking out, just in case."

79
00:04:58.343 --> 00:05:01.205
All four of them hurried past the house to the backyard.

80
00:05:02.787 --> 00:05:05.709
Then they climbed up the ladder leading into Nathan's tree house.

81
00:05:05.729 --> 00:05:09.473
"Wow," Cole said, looking around.

82
00:05:09.493 --> 00:05:12.695
"This place is really cool, Nathan!

83
00:05:13.716 --> 00:05:15.618
You can see half the neighborhood from up here."

84
00:05:16.639 --> 00:05:18.600
Henry wasn't very interested in the view.

85
00:05:19.661 --> 00:05:22.224
He was busy looking around for anything suspicious.

86
00:05:23.424 --> 00:05:27.726
But all he saw were some empty candy wrappers and Nathan's favorite comic books.

87
00:05:28.827 --> 00:05:31.989
There was no sign that Nora had been in the tree house recently.

88
00:05:32.009 --> 00:05:35.050
"Oh well," Henry said.

89
00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:37.892
"I guess this idea isn't working.

90
00:05:39.012 --> 00:05:42.014
Maybe we'll have to wait until tonight to try another stakeout."

91
00:05:42.034 --> 00:05:46.296
"Okay," Maggie said, and Nathan nodded.

92
00:05:47.177 --> 00:05:48.277
Cole wasn't listening.

93
00:05:49.218 --> 00:05:50.699
He was still looking out the window.

94
00:05:50.719 --> 00:05:52.379
"Hey, check it out!"

95
00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:53.140
he said.

96
00:05:54.025 --> 00:05:58.278
"Nora just climbed out the playroom window again and is sneaking across the yard!"
